# Reference Library

When the user asks for an architectural / urban-planning drawing, consult
the following sources **before** drawing. They are the authoritative
documents for projects on this machine.

## Legislation & standards (PDF / DOCX)

Folder: `C:\Users\PCZONE.GE\Downloads\wetransfer_03_xref_saproeqto_2026-04-29_1038\kanonmdebloba\`

| File                                        | What it covers |
|---------------------------------------------|----------------|
| `14-39.pdf` + `_konsolodirebuli*.pdf`       | Tbilisi land-use main ordinance #14-39 |
| `41.pdf`                                    | Tbilisi ordinance #41 |
| `57.pdf`                                    | Tbilisi ordinance #57 |
| `59.pdf`                                    | Tbilisi ordinance #59 |
| `4-13_*.pdf`                                | Document #4-13 + amendments |
| `N41 dadgenileba shezguduli...pdf`          | Accessibility requirements (disabled persons) |
| `grg ...pdf`                                | GRG (general plan) procedural rules |
| `СНиП 2.07.01-89.pdf`                       | Soviet/Russian urban-planning code (rooms, distances, parking) |
| `National CAD Standard ver 3.1.pdf`         | NCS 3.1 — layer naming, sheet codes, line weights |
| `Neufert.Architects.Data.3rd.ed.2000.pdf`   | THE architectural data reference (room sizes, ergonomics) |
| `Raumpilot-Grundlagen / -Wohnen / -Arbeiten / -Lernen.pdf` | German residential / work / learning typologies |

When a request is ambiguous (e.g. "draw a school plan"), pull dimensions
from Neufert + Raumpilot, and zoning constraints from the Tbilisi
ordinances.

