  `xref_rekr`, `xref_samsh_arasamsh`, `xref_servituti`, `xref_shenoba`,
  `xref_sxivebi`, `xref_topo`, `xref_zonreba`, `xref_miwisqvesha_avtosadgomebi`.
- Output PDFs follow the **GRG to PDF-XX.pdf** naming where XX is the
  sheet code (A1–A8, CIG, CIP, CIS, CIW, CIR1, CIR2, CTS12, CVC4,
  CZLSZ, CZVCNZ, FZ1–FZ8, MZLFZ, MZLSZ, MZLTSZ).

When the user says "make a GRG sheet for FZ3", use the same filename
pattern, the same xref structure, and the title block `01-title-block.mdc`
specifies.

## How to use this index

1. Identify the **drawing type** the user wants (zoning, GRG, building plan, section).
2. Match to the closest reference DWG above and reuse its layer/xref structure.
3. If no DWG matches, fall back to Neufert / Raumpilot / СНиП for sizing,
   then the Tbilisi ordinances for setbacks, heights, FAR, K-coefficients.
4. Sheet labels and codes always follow the existing project codes
   (`კ-…`, `A-…`, `FZ-…`, `CZ…`, `MZL…`).
